# Root .dockerignore. It applies ONLY to the `web` image, whose build context is
# the repo root (docker-compose.yml web.build.context) so it can bundle docs/.
# The api image builds from its own subdir context (./api) with its own
# .dockerignore, so nothing here affects it.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-07-17 (PRD #58 M6): this used to say the AGENT image also builds
# "from its own subdir context (./agent)". It does not, and has not since PRD #39
# Decision 5 — its context is the REPO ROOT (docker-compose.yml agent.build.context
# is `.`), because the worker image bakes uzi's own source at /opt/uzi-src for the
# `chat` run kind. agent/.dockerignore is a leftover of the old subdir context and
# is read by nothing.
#
# So this file is NOT irrelevant to the agent — it is the FALLBACK it must never
# reach. What actually trims the agent context is the per-Dockerfile ignore next to
# each template (agent/templates/<t>/Dockerfile.dockerignore), which both BuildKit
# and kaniko prefer over this file (kaniko v1.24.0 pkg/util/fs_util.go:777 tries
# "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" first and only then the context root's). That
# precedence is load-bearing: the `agent/` exclusion below would break the agent
# build outright (its Dockerfile COPYs agent/package.json), so deleting a template's
# named ignore does not merely widen its context — it breaks the build.
#
# Load-bearing: this must NOT blanket-exclude *.md (the way web/.dockerignore
# does) — docs/*.md are exactly the files the web image bundles. The web/
# .dockerignore no longer applies once the context is the repo root.

# VCS + never-needed-in-any-image
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules

# Secrets must never enter a build context — including a dev-local one nested in
# a subdir (e.g. web/.env). The bare patterns only match the root; the `**/`
# globs catch any depth.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Submodules and sibling services the web build does not need. inspiration/ is
# large; api/ builds from its own context; e2e/ is test-only. `agent/` is excluded
# for the WEB image only — the agent image shares this context root but is trimmed
# by its own per-Dockerfile ignore instead (see the header), never by this file.
inspiration/
api/
agent/
e2e/

# Web build artifacts / installed deps (regenerated by `npm ci` in the image).
web/node_modules
web/dist
